  "split_decision": "Copy only the entire independent optional natural data or whole endomap/fixed-predicate component. Preserve mixed own-provider schemas and genuine property proofs in exact archives rather than narrow records, add missing laws or create a legacy self-provider import.",
  "review_notes": [
    "Filtration genuinely supplies Carrier : Type _ and step : Nat -> Type _, but no inclusion map into Carrier, nesting relation, union or intersection. Exhaustive and separated are independent chosen propositions with genuine supplied proof fields, not equations about the step family.",
    "HodgeDeRhamFiltration retains all original C/F dependencies, actual supplied Filtration data, an independent associatedConnection proposition/proof, unproved degeneratesAtE1? : Prop and harmonicBasis? : Option Type. No actual connection relation or basis property is encoded.",
    "All three theorem bodies genuinely project their selected proof fields under their exact original hypotheses. Preserve the proofs without interpreting their names as analytic, Hodge-de Rham, spectral-sequence or conditional-expectation results.",
    "Both complete mixed schemas and all three genuine proof commands remain in exact archives. Extracting pure subsets would drop fields or narrow types; extracting own-provider consequences would require a new historical self-import. Neither is introduced.",
    "The organized Probability.ConditionalExpectation classification is lexical history, not a verified probability structure. Original documentation, notices and unresolved import identity are retained."
  ],
